# 1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Modify and enhance my existing working FloodGuard application into a complete AI-powered, community-driven flood-risk intelligence and emergency safe-route management platform.

FloodGuard should help citizens make informed evacuation and emergency decisions while enabling authorised disaster-management experts to monitor flood risks, manage incidents, analyse road conditions and coordinate emergency response.

The application must have TWO COMPLETELY SEPARATE INTERFACES:

1. CITIZEN MODE – Personal emergency assistance and safe-route navigation.
2. EXPERT MODE – Secure flood monitoring, disaster management and operational decision support.

Both interfaces must use shared backend services, datasets, database records, flood-risk calculations and routing algorithms.

**IMPORTANT: The existing application is already developed and working.**

Do not rebuild the project from scratch.

Before modifying anything:
- Inspect the existing project structure.
- Understand the current frontend and backend.
- Identify existing components and working features.
- Inspect database schemas and APIs.
- Identify the existing routing implementation.
- Identify existing authentication functionality.
- Reuse existing components wherever possible.

Preserve the current FloodGuard branding, dark theme, map implementation, working functionality and technology stack.

Do not replace functional components unnecessarily.

Default geographical scope: Pune and Pimpri-Chinchwad, Maharashtra, India.

Keep the system modular so additional geographical areas can be added later.

